{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-183812",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14259374/assets/1b3a9a3891150ae0b187c79e2305d391f719898a9efe42b42e7bf0777d965aa3.png)\n\nFor a random variable $Z∼N(0,1)$ we have the following symmetry property for $a>0:$\n\n$$\nP(Z>-a)=P(Z<a)=Φ(a)\n$$\n\nWe're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z<2.22).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14259374/assets/2efe9f4a4ac7f5bc307ef3e13d5f53f39be0143de2f33d87887235bc37410c94.png)\n\nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z>-2.22).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14259374/assets/94537e936e6fcb151fb8d61a3cd118bc8b1caaa609777c2eb0d363fc1063c885.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z<2.22) & =P(Z>-2.22) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<-2.22) \\\\  & =1-Φ(-2.22) \\\\  & =1-0.0132 \\\\  & =0.9868.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-183812\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><div id=\"graphic-ed6cf0f80f9a77077c775e722675a76b\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/ed6cf0f80f9a77077c775e722675a76b\"></div>\n\n<p>For a random variable <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"213\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D44D TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c223C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D441 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> we have the following symmetry property for <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"214\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D44E TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-texatom></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><m